From 131a8e2ec63f61ff3e15fbd7f5820c2c3b5f035e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmad Jalil <ahzs645@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:03:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(indoor): door-scoped native-cell owner review as a
 regeneration source review

Adds --native-door-owner-review FILE to regenerate-from-native-cache.ts and
NATIVE_DOOR_OWNER_REVIEW to the recompile run.sh, modelled on the door
aperture review and the boundary patch review. Unset, the regeneration runs
exactly as before: no compiler option is passed and nothing else changes.

The file (source-native-door-owner-review-v1) lists native doors and the two
rooms each should join. It can carry no tolerance, geometry or access
decision; unknown fields are refused. Only the listed doors are affected.

scripts/indoor/source-native-door-owner-review.ts refuses before the compile
starts when the model digest differs, a room is not a walkable area on the
door's level, a reviewed door link already names the door, the door has no
precise footprint and normal, or the legacy matcher already pairs it. The
source rooms are not changed. The native cells exist only inside the compile,
so Reviter makes the final decision at door matching and aborts the compile
unless the native-cell matcher, with its default 2 ft owner gap, finds exactly
the two listed rooms.

The regeneration copies the review to source-native-door-owner-review.json
and writes source-native-door-owner-replay.json as soon as the last listed
door is applied: door, native sides, cell ids and bounds, owner gaps in feet,
applied rooms and the review digests. regeneration.json records the review
when the flag is given.

Requires the Reviter commit that adds nativeDoorOwnerReview to
prepareIndoorDataset. The runtime binding fingerprints are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
